---
import AppPageLayout from "../../../layouts/AppPageLayout.astro";
---

<AppPageLayout
  app="TolaVR Player"
  title="Support"
  description="Help for TolaVR Player, the VR video player for Apple Vision Pro."
>
  <p>
    TolaVR Player is a VR video player for Apple Vision Pro. Need help? Email
    <a href="mailto:support@megakad.com">support@megakad.com</a> and we'll get back to you.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting started</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open a website with a VR video in TolaVR Player's browser and press play on the site's video.</li>
    <li>When “Video found” appears, tap <strong>Play in VR</strong>.</li>
    <li>Tap the video to show the controls. Tap ✕ above the controls to go back to the browser.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>The picture looks doubled or uncomfortable.</strong> The format may be wrong. Use the View
    button to pick 180° or 360°, and side by side, top/bottom or flat. Your choice is remembered for
    that video.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>I'm lying down and the video is in the wrong place.</strong> Look where you want the video and
    hold the Digital Crown, or use Recenter. The bed button has sitting, reclined and lying presets.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>The video looks blurry.</strong> Use the Quality button to pick a higher resolution if the site
    offers one. VR video needs 6K–8K to look sharp.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>“Only a small preview found”.</strong> Press play on the video itself on the web page, then try
    again.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>A video won't play.</strong> Some sites protect their videos with DRM, which TolaVR Player
    can't play.
  </p>
</AppPageLayout>
